# =============================================================================
# .gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This repository tracks BOTH the Expo frontend AND the Node backend, because
# the backend is deployed from git (see render.yaml -> startCommand:
#   node --experimental-sqlite backend/server.mjs).
#
# Vercel only builds the Expo web frontend (npm run build -> expo export) and
# never bundles backend/ (the frontend does not import it), so SOURCE trees are
# intentionally NOT ignored here. Only local / runtime artifacts are ignored.
#
# (The previous revision ignored whole source trees such as `backend/`, `data/`
#  and `test/`. That silently dropped every newly added backend module and test
#  from version control — which would have broken the Render deploy, since the
#  backend server imports those modules at boot. Fixed.)
# =============================================================================

# --- Dependencies & tooling caches -------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.expo/
.expo-shared/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Runtime data (SQLite database + agent workspace) — never commit ---------
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
backend/data/

# --- Archives (never shipped in git) -----------------------------------------
*.zip

# --- Local secrets (defence in depth — real values are never committed) ------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- OS / editor noise -------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
